 "dates": "Monday, November 9 – Sunday, November 15, 2009",
 "logline": "A bill comes due, home calls at one in the morning, somebody stays to the end of a song, and a week is up.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Becca asked if she could tell her mother you’re her boyfriend. You didn’t say no.",
   "if": "becca_official"
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo, in the dark, at one in the morning: “Costigan. Are you happy?”",
   "if": "!becca_knows_lena_ask && e14_happy"
  },
  {
   "text": "You told Becca you’re going to ask Lena home for Thanksgiving. She zipped her lips: “It’s yours to ask. I’m not *allowed*.”",
   "if": "becca_knows_lena_ask"
  },
  {
   "text": "Walking home at one in the morning, Lena said she’d go anywhere on Thanksgiving where nobody knows his name. You decided to ask her to Youngstown — properly, in a week.",
   "if": "jack_plans_ask_lena"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your mother: “Then Christmas! Bring her at Christmas.” And, lower: “Your father’s in the garage a lot.”",
   "if": "maria_wants_becca_xmas"
  },
  {
   "text": "Julian asked Lena to Bastille on Thursday, to hear his new song. He told her you promised to stay to the end.",
   "if": "lena_julian_bastille"
  },
  {
   "text": "“Ask me again in a week. —L.”",
   "if": "e14_danny"
  }
 ],
